{"hw":"Αἴας","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">Αἴας</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">Αἴας</span>, <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">αντος</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ajax</cite>, masc. pr. n., borne by two heroes, the Greater, son of Telamon, the Less, son of Oiïleus, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hom.</span> </span>:—nom. <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <span class=\"gk\">Αἶας</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Alcm.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">68</span> </span>; voc. <span class=\"gk\">Αἶαν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">184</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Aeol.</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">Αἴαν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Alc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">48</span> </span> A: pl. <span class=\"gk\">Αἴαντες</span>, of tragedies named after Ajax, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Po.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1455b34</span> </span>. (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> </span> derives it fancifully from <span class=\"gk\">αἰαῖ</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Aj.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">430</span> </span>.)</div></div>"}